From 720c90e4cbc3f347d4fa3b292a1e761affe33b14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lionel Debieve <lionel.debieve@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Dec 2021 14:51:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 0526/1695] plat-stm32mp1: add low power drivers for stm32mp1

Implements system suspend/resume for STM32MP1 when board supports
STPMIC1. Defines boolean configuration switch CFG_PM to embed or not
PM (standby) support.

STMP32MP15 implements a specific sequence to encrypt and sign TEE RAM
(SYSRAM) content in DDR at suspend and restore it at resume.

OP-TEE uses a piece or secure retention memory to store information
when suspending and have BL2 bootstage use them to resume the system.

Adds config switch CFG_STM32MP1_OPTEE_IN_SYSRAM that defines if
STM32MP1 OP-TEE executes in internal RAM with pager. When disabled,
OP-TEE low power sequence relies on TF-A BL2 resident service left
in SYSRAM. When CFG_STM32MP1_OPTEE_IN_SYSRAM is enabled, the low power
suspend sequence in fully implemented in OP-TEE.

